/**
 * The `font-variant-numeric` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
 * controls the usage of alternate glyphs for numbers, fractions, and ordinal markers.
 *
 * Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - diagonal-fractions: Enables display of lining diagonal fractions.
 * - lining-nums: Enables display of lining numerals.
 * - normal: This keyword leads to the deactivation of the use of such alternate glyphs.
 * - oldstyle-nums: Enables display of old-style numerals.
 * - ordinal: This keyword forces the use of special glyphs for the ordinal markers, like 1st, 2nd,
 * 3rd, 4th in English or a 1a in Italian. It corresponds to the OpenType values `ordn`.
 * - proportional-nums: Enables display of proportional numerals.
 * - slashed-zero: This keyword forces the use of a 0 with a slash; this is useful when a clear
 * distinction between O and 0 is needed. It corresponds to the OpenType values `zero`.
 * - stacked-fractions: Enables display of lining stacked fractions.
 * - tabular-nums: Enables display of tabular numerals.
 *
 * Grammar: normal | [ <numeric-figure-values> || <numeric-spacing-values> ||
 * <numeric-fraction-values> || ordinal || slashed-zero ]
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-variant-numeric
 *
 * Author guide:
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-variant-numeric
 *
 * Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
 *
 * Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
 *
 * Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.
 */
